+simplicial triangulation of $B^3$.
+For $k>1$, the new tet may meet $\tau_{k-1}$ in one, two, or three
+faces.  In the shellings obtained below, the three-face move does not
+occur; equivalently, the number of boundary vertices never decreases.
+Call $\tau$ \emph{freely shellable} if any tet of $\tau$ can be chosen as
+the first tet of such a shelling.
 
 \begin{theorem} \label{th3}
 If $\sigma$ is a simplicial triangulation of $S^2$,
-any taut filling $\tau$ of $\sigma$
-is a freely monotone shellable
+any taut filling of $X(\sigma)$ is a freely shellable
